bythepond-by-tkln for Debian
----------------------------

Upstream only ships the intro as a self-extracting compressed shell script
(by_the_pond_by_tkln.sh on scene.org, see debian/copyright). The orig
tarball contains the executable extracted from this script, with the
fullscreen flag removed from the SDL_SetVideoMode call so that the intro
starts in a window.

The executable is only linked to libdl and libc: libGL.so.1 and
libSDL-1.2.so.0 are opened at run time with dlopen, so they are declared
by hand in the Depends field of debian/control. It has no section header
table and must not be stripped (see debian/rules).

executable seems to be compiled for an unknown distribution: the binary is
packed, it contains no compiler identification string.

(no output from: strings -a by_the_pond_by_tkln | grep -i gcc)

Source files:
-------------
(none listed by elfls -cd: no symbol table)

